checks_run.procedure:
Confirm the frozen candidate:
- check the assignment's sha256;
- recompute the candidate ID in the repository, and in the disposable clone after the runs with the probe copy moved out;
- confirm that HEAD is the freeze commit on top of source_commit and that only delivery records changed since;
- run the DG1 historical validation.

On a fresh disposable stack (PG16 UTF8 + API, synthetic seed), create transformations and walk Diagnose→Define→Design through the API as dev.lead/dev.office/dev.admin:
- modes and the B0018 roles;
- B0023 gate names and sequential G1→G2→G3 (out-of-sequence refused);
- T01 six dimensions with H/M/L confidence, the six B0029 workstreams and the ten B0056 dimensions;
- the 14-field charter with versions, the composed four-part B0037 thesis (incomplete when a part is blank or invisible-only), and the five B0039-B0043 scope checks;
- one current North Star, the 3-5 outcome warning, the good-outcome test and guardrails (G2 blocked at zero);
- T02 target date;
- the TOM canvas (ten boxes, B0062 prompts; ready needs target and owner) and G3 blocked until the gap matrix, capability gaps and future journeys exist;
- live G1, G2 and G3 decisions;
- Arabic charter text with RLM/ALM accepted verbatim, and invisible-only values refused (validation.blank) across fields.

New probe for D-071 / T-DG2-BE16, from the domain angle:
- a 2 MiB evidence file with an Arabic file name (RLM, emoji) is uploaded over a raw keep-alive socket, and a second request is sent on the same socket;
- the file is downloaded and compared byte for byte;
- a 26 MiB upload (over the 25 MiB limit) is streamed: check the declared refusal, Connection: close, the time until the server closes the socket, that no revision is added and that the previous content is unchanged;
- the EN/AR localized message is checked;
- a normal upload after the refusal is checked;
- SPA deep links (Diagnose/Define/Design, served by the not-found handler that is now rate-metered) and an unknown API address are checked;
- product gate codes are listed.

Re-run my earlier-round API probes unchanged as regressions:
- r10-delta-api (D-070 media types, Arabic verbatim, invisible-only refusal, localized validation.content_type, gate codes);
- regress-d069-api (binary evidence round trip, content-type refusals);
- regress-d068, regress-d067 and regress-d066 (earlier text and validation repairs).

In Chromium on a fresh stack, EN (LTR) and AR (RTL):
- a charter with Arabic text containing RLM and emoji is created through the UI and read back;
- a malformed request's form-level problem is shown once;
- an evidence file is uploaded through the UI (the request content type is captured) and the download is compared byte for byte, with the Arabic file name suggested.

In Chromium, EN and AR:
- invisible-only, default-ignorable-only and spaces-only Case for change values on charter create are refused inline with the localized message, aria-invalid and focus, and nothing is sent;
- visible text is accepted verbatim;
- the thesis shows Incomplete with four empty parts;
- an invisible-only Out of scope on edit is refused and no version is written.
Then re-run the regress-d067/d066 UI probes.

New probe. In Chromium, EN and AR, for one synthetic transformation, open Diagnose, Define, Design, Gates, the G1 detail and Evidence:
- check html lang/dir and that each page renders (not the not-found page);
- check that no text claims PMI certification or official Mobily branding and none names DG0-DG7;
- check the gate names on Gates (B0023 EN; Arabic names AR) and the provisional wordmark.
Inspect the screenshots.

checks_run.actual:
